{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378888-mt3zWlPU4lnS2RcuM8ai","role":"assistant","created":1775378898,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see numpy isn't available. Let me calculate the Fisher excess kurtosis manually or use a different approach.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_bc06d8ffdb4b4574b2deacd4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Paper money in circulation data from FY 1941 to FY 1950\n# Using values from the Treasury Bulletins (in millions of dollars):\n# FY 1941: 8932 (from 1948 bulletin)\n# FY 1942: 11600 (from 1948 bulletin)\n# FY 1943: 16492 (both bulletins)\n# FY 1944: 21438 (both bulletins)\n# FY 1945: 25541 (from 1948 bulletin) vs 25511 (from 1950 bulletin)\n# Let me check which one to use...\n\n# Actually for consistency, I should use the 1948 bulletin for years 1941-1948 \n# since that's the primary source for those years\n\n# Let me recalculate with 1948 bulletin values:\ndata_1948 = [8932, 11600, 16492, 21438, 25541, 26945, 26942, 26482]\n\n# And 1950 bulletin for 1949-1950:\n# 1949: 26034\n# 1950: 25661\n\n# Combined: FY 1941-1950\ndata = [8932, 11600, 16492, 21438, 25541, 26945, 26942, 26482, 26034, 25661]\n\nprint(\"Paper money in circulation (millions of dollars) - FY 1941-1950:\")\nfor i, (year, val) in enumerate(zip(range(1941, 1951), data)):\n    print(f\"FY {year}: {val}\")\n\n# Calculate unbiased sample Fisher excess kurtosis manually\n# Formula: g2 = [(n+1)*m4 / (m2^2) - 3*(n-1)] / ((n-2)*(n-3)) * (n-1) + 3\n# where m2 = second moment about mean, m4 = fourth moment about mean\n\nn = len(data)\nmean = sum(data) / n\n\n# Calculate moments about the mean\nm2 = sum((x - mean)**2 for x in data) / n  # second moment\nm4 = sum((x - mean)**4 for x in data) / n  # fourth moment\n\nprint(f\"\\nn = {n}\")\nprint(f\"Mean = {mean}\")\n\n# Unbiased estimator for excess kurtosis (Fisher's formula)\n# Using the formula: g2 = ((n+1)*n*m4 / ((n-1)*(n-2)*(n-3)*m2^2)) - 3*(n-1)^2 / ((n-2)*(n-3))\n# Another form: g2 = ((n+1)*m4 / m2**2 - 3*(n-1)) / ((n-2)*(n-3)) * (n-1) + 3\n\n# Let's use the standard formula for unbiased sample excess kurtosis:\n# g2 = [(n+1)*n*m4 / ((n-1)*(n-2)*(n-3)*m2^2)] - 3*(n-1)^2 / ((n-2)*(n-3))\n\ng2 = ((n+1) * n * m4 / ((n-1) * (n-2) * (n-3) * m2**2)) - (3 * (n-1)**2) / ((n-2) * (n-3))\n\nprint(f\"\\nm2 = {m2}\")\nprint(f\"m4 = {m4}\")\nprint(f\"\\nUnbiased sample Fisher excess Kurtosis: {g2}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 3 decimal places: {round(g2, 3)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
